{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons","id":1268456,"title":"Debate Valkyries Vampiric patrons.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-17T19:29:10-08:00","id":1268456,"title":"Debate Valkyries Vampiric patrons.","content":"its come to my attention that some seriously dislike the whole &quot;Secretly manipulated by vampires&quot; aspect of Valkyrie, thought id ask on it.<br /> <br /> I like it personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T21:55:56-08:00","id":1268478,"title":"","content":"Originator of the joke/semi-serious fan theory of &quot;Led by Vampire Abe Lincoln&quot; here. Less known as the &quot;Also Loki-trying-to-change-fate-somehow&quot; theorist. (Together, they are codenamed Stovepipe and Shears)<br /> <br /> You can take a guess how I feel about it.<br /> <br /> (but seriously, I do I like it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T02:20:28-08:00","id":1268498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons#post1268456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">its come to my attention that some seriously dislike the whole &quot;Secretly manipulated by vampires&quot; aspect of Valkyrie, thought id ask on it.<br /> <br /> I like it personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's the idea itself as much as it's how undeveloped it is. Like, Night Stalkers merely heavily hints at it, which would be fine, and that's how that kind of thing would usually be handled. However C&amp;C actually point-blank tells you the answer, but then doesn't actually tell you anything, there aren't even some interesting elaborations like the Cheiron Board have.<br /> <br /> I vaguely remember hearing that there was a more elaborate backstory cut for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T03:42:58-08:00","id":1268509,"title":"","content":"The whole point of Hunter is humans fighting back. Having prominent conspiracies like Valkyrie be headed by non human entities kind of cheapens the purpose and make the Hunters look like a bunch of fools being manipulated by the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","user":"Apex Predator","date":". 11-18-2018, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","name":"Apex Predator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T16:20:10-08:00","id":1268660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apex Predator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268509#post1268509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of Hunter is humans fighting back. Having prominent conspiracies like Valkyrie be headed by non human entities kind of cheapens the purpose and make the Hunters look like a bunch of fools being manipulated by the supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the entire point of Conspiracies is that they are compromised.<br /> <br /> I mean, Valkyrie being <i>funded </i>by vampires(and that's important to distinguish, they are funded by vamps and expected to act in response to that rather than simply being run by them) is small potatoes compared to<br /> <br /> Actively Act In the Abyss's Favor to Keep It Quiet(Knights of St. George),<br /> Act as the Spirit's Ambassadors and Soldiers in the Conflict over the Border(Les Mysteres),<br /> Probably a Puppet for VII[Whatever the fuck they are](Cainite Heresy),<br /> Pretty Much Absolutely the Result of Shuankhsen Efforts(Feast of Shulpae),<br /> Has a God-Machine Angel as Their Driving Client(Knights of St. Adrian),<br /> Posers as Government Agents for the Panopticon(Division Six[compact, but worth mentioning]),<br /> Run by Extra-Dimensional Entities who Either Have Odd Ideas About Fighting the Apocalypse or Terrifying Ideas About Causing the Apocalypse and Oh By The Way Are Capitalist Fucks(Cheiron Group),<br /> Actively Serve an Actively Angry and Gluttonous Ghoul and are Possibly Powered by Really Warped Imitator of a God Who Is Already A Fuck(Malleus Maleficarum),<br /> Operate Under Probable-Metaphysical Gunpoint of a Woman of Indeterminate Origin(Lucifuge),<br /> Probably Manipulated by a Number of Ghost Conspiracies(Council of Bones)<br /> Probably and Inexplicably Linked to the Fairy Order of Oneirophysics (Asclepion)<br /> Likely An Extended Cult for the Deceived (Enigmatics)<br /> Probably Half-Directed by Either a Changeling or a Demon or a Demon in a Changeling's Cover (Operation Nebula)<br /> A Bunch of Near-Slashers Commiting to Acts Likely To Make Them Full-Slashers (Survivor's Club)<br /> I'm Not Sure What Arisen Bullshit This Is Exactly, But It's Some Kind of Arisen-Adjacent Bullshit, Unless It's Astral Bullshit, Or Both (Watchers)\u200b<br /> and Might Probably be Manipulated by the Most Judgmental Morally Grey Folks in Mage's Setup(Aegis Kai Doru).<br /> <br /> One of Hunter's points is that the road to power has more than a price, but a challenge, nay, a <i>compromise</i> to one's sense of correct action-one's sense of moral, ethical, even <i>existential</i> validity will come under fire the more one operates <i>as</i> a hunter. It's the cost of doing business.<br /> <br /> On a positive side, it reinforces the similarities between humanity and their monsters. Valkyrie, ironically, does this best-for all that Valkyrie would flip on it's head to find out about who is funding their alientation-through-access-to-advanced-technology-and-governmental-validation, it's also the easiest place to see where the concerns of humanity and monsters are most in line(namely that the best operating state for both sides is in the Masquerade of Ignorance Feigned), and how from there we can work in tandem with one another to build a better world. While it's easy to see the problems with such in all the others, it also stands as similar proofs-Conspiracies are where the concept of the Human/Monster divide gets to fall apart and we begin to consider the possibility that there are better symbioses that can be developed for the benefit of everyone.<br /> <br /> On the negative side...<br /> <br /> Welp. The Road to Power is Where Virtue Dies. You want to make a change, you had better be willing to sacrifice some of your ideals on the altar of the dark for the benefit of the other ones. Hope you know which ones are worth it, because if you don't, the end of the day sees you as a puppet to the monsters you were fighting and a slave the darkness you hoped to overcome.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Hunter. You're not the good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-22-2023, 06:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T16:36:15-08:00","id":1268664,"title":"","content":"I think they want to show for other games, especial requiem that you CAN create and run a Cancer conspiracy if you want.<br /> then again I have a LOW opinion of the government.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-18-2018, 07:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T01:24:39-08:00","id":1268756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268660#post1268660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the entire point of Conspiracies is that they are compromised.<br /> <br /> I mean, Valkyrie being <i>funded </i>by vampires(and that's important to distinguish, they are funded by vamps and expected to act in response to that rather than simply being run by them) is small potatoes compared to<br /> <br /> Actively Act In the Abyss's Favor to Keep It Quiet(Knights of St. George),<br /> Act as the Spirit's Ambassadors and Soldiers in the Conflict over the Border(Les Mysteres),<br /> Probably a Puppet for VII[Whatever the fuck they are](Cainite Heresy),<br /> Pretty Much Absolutely the Result of Shuankhsen Efforts(Feast of Shulpae),<br /> Has a God-Machine Angel as Their Driving Client(Knights of St. Adrian),<br /> Posers as Government Agents for the Panopticon(Division Six[compact, but worth mentioning]),<br /> Run by Extra-Dimensional Entities who Either Have Odd Ideas About Fighting the Apocalypse or Terrifying Ideas About Causing the Apocalypse and Oh By The Way Are Capitalist Fucks(Cheiron Group), <br /> Actively Serve an Actively Angry and Gluttonous Ghoul and are Possibly Powered by Really Warped Imitator of a God Who Is Already A Fuck(Malleus Maleficarum),<br /> Operate Under Probable-Metaphysical Gunpoint of a Woman of Indeterminate Origin(Lucifuge),<br /> and Might Probably be Manipulated by the Most Judgmental Morally Grey Folks in Mage's Setup(Aegis Kai Doru).<br /> <br /> One of Hunter's points is that the road to power has more than a price, but a challenge, nay, a <i>compromise</i> to one's sense of correct action-one's sense of moral, ethical, even <i>existential</i> validity will come under fire the more one operates <i>as</i> a hunter. It's the cost of doing business.<br /> <br /> On a positive side, it reinforces the similarities between humanity and their monsters. Valkyrie, ironically, does this best-for all that Valkyrie would flip on it's head to find out about who is funding their alientation-through-access-to-advanced-technology-and-governmental-validation, it's also the easiest place to see where the concerns of humanity and monsters are most in line(namely that the best operating state for both sides is in the Masquerade of Ignorance Feigned), and how from there we can work in tandem with one another to build a better world. While it's easy to see the problems with such in all the others, it also stands as similar proofs-Conspiracies are where the concept of the Human/Monster divide gets to fall apart and we begin to consider the possibility that there are better symbioses that can be developed for the benefit of everyone.<br /> <br /> On the negative side...<br /> <br /> Welp. The Road to Power is Where Virtue Dies. You want to make a change, you had better be willing to sacrifice some of your ideals on the altar of the dark for the benefit of the other ones. Hope you know which ones are worth it, because if you don't, the end of the day sees you as a puppet to the monsters you were fighting and a slave the darkness you hoped to overcome.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Hunter. You're not the good guys.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a fan of that. I think part of the reason behind Hunter is to balance the &quot;Monsters Runs the Party&quot; theme in the world of darkness; to show that humans can fight back no matter the cost or consequences.<br /> <br /> The whole &quot;Monster behind every Conspiracy&quot; reduces Hunters to little more than hit squads. Also, disminishes their responsability over the Vigil's ugly truth: that humans themselves can be as bad as the supernatural menaces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:00:50-08:00","id":1268775,"title":"","content":"Vampires having a hand in Task Force: Vaklyrie and manipulating it for its purposes is one thing. The thole thing being no more than another goon squad for powerful vampires is another. It's all a matter of degrees. Hunters being manipulated, controlled and compromised by monsters is inevitable. But do it too much and the whole point of the gameline is lost. Hunter is special because while the entire rest of the Chronicles of Darkness treats mortals as background and collateral damage, Hunter gives them teeth. Making conspiracies just another pawn of the supernatural puts a hole in it. <br /> <br /> I also heavily dispute the claim that the &quot;point&quot; of Conspiracies is to be compromised. Conspiracies provide hunters with a chain of command, resources, knowledge and a supernatural edge.But they're mired in their ideology, corrupt and often questionably better than the monsters they hunt. All that can be accomplished by humans. No need for supernatural manipulation. Hunter is about mortal humans doing things on their own, for better or (frequently) worse. Let's let hunter organizations do or die on their own, without having supernaturals run everything just like in every other CofD game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:49:43-08:00","id":1268784,"title":"","content":"Saying that every conspiracy is compromised is a bit of a stretch- but that depends on how you define &quot;being compromised&quot;. For example, sure the Lucifuge is ruled by a very questionable person, but every member of the conspiracy is, in fact, a monster, which is the defining trait of the organization. Are the Lucifuge compromised because of that? Many hunters would say &quot;Of course! Kill the devil spawn!&quot;, but I assume that many of the less zealot members would question that. The MM is controlled by a ghoul- but ghouls are still human, and he does hunts other vampires and actively supports the Vigil. Is he a monster? Yes. Does the Malleus compromised because of that? Again, depends on who you ask. Sure, some conspiracies are much more into the dark side than others (The Knights of St George which appease sleeping gods, the Mysteres which serve the spirit world, the Cainte Heresy which blindly work for unknown patrons, etc, etc), but even they have their redeeming qualities (usually). The Cainte, for example, would kill vampires- they are manipulated, and they know they are manipulated, but they simply don't care as long as it allows them to kill those creatures they hate so much. The Mysteres serve the spirits- but again, they are aware of their manipulations, and they know that the alternatives is just let them roam free and do as they wish. The Faithful of Shulpae may use an heretic ceremony for power, but they still hunt monsters instead of serving them (sure, you may say that they serve the ultimate force of entropy, but that's about as sinful as polluting, and no one is called a &quot;monster&quot; for that). Cheiron Group may be controlled by alien entities, but one of the options is that while their methods are dangerous and dreadful, they still work for the Vigil in their own way.<br /> <br /> In short, here is the thing- most of the conspiracies use some short of supernatural trick. Usually, supernatural tricks require supernatural help. Supernatural help usually comes in the form of monsters. So yeah, hunters use tools of questionable origin in order to hunt monsters. Does that mean they are compromised? Some hunters would say yes, others would say no. Some conspiracies don't even have that- the Ascending Ones, for example, have dark sides, but those are human evils, not monstrous ones. The AKD may have desires to rise above their mortal status, but they are still humans. VASCU, as weird as it may be, is the most honest conspiracy, where players have argued again and again about the fact that the weirdest thing about them is that they have nothing weird about them (with the exception of the Hall of Mirrors and that line about the Director which &quot;works non stop&quot; that many just wish to take it literally).<br /> <br /> So yeah, Valkyrie is funded by vampires. And yes, those vampires sometimes use their influence in order to get rid of their enemies or help their friends. Do they control the conspiracy as whole? Not so much. Valkyrie hunts more than vampires, after all, and the ST is the ones to decide how far does the corruption goes in the organization. Plus, that whole angle exists mostly for the players to explore a situation where they discover Valkyrie's unseen supporters, and have to decide what to do with that- something like the SHIELD vs HYDRA conflict in the Winter Soldier. Conspiracies as whole examine the grey line between hunters and monsters, and force you to ask questions about what price you are willing to pay in order to fight the darkness. Asking &quot;what is a monster&quot; and &quot;can a monster be redeemed&quot; is something that Hunter as whole is meant to ask- conspiracies simply take it to the next level, where you either touch the boundary yourself, or that you work with lesser evils in order to defeat greater ones- or for profit. Or for some other form of personal gain.<br /> <br /> Yes, you know that you are manipulated. Yes, you know that it is not a perfect solution- but this is not a perfect world. You have seen it in your own eyes. But in spite of it- or because of it- every light counts. Every candle can bring hope to a better world. The question is how much are you willing to pay, and if the shadows the candle cast are deeper than the darkness it was meant to lite. Hunter was never a game of good vs evil- it is a game of grey lines and questionable choices, of small lights and deeper darkness, which all settles up to the moment where you lay in a back street, covered in your own blood and look to the sky as the life leaves your body while you ask &quot;was it all worth it?&quot;, and all you can do is to hope that in that moment, and answer will be &quot;yes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-19-2018, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:21:26-08:00","id":1268806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268784#post1268784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, that whole angle exists mostly for the players to explore a situation where they discover Valkyrie's unseen supporters, and have to decide what to do with that- something like the SHIELD vs HYDRA conflict in the Winter Soldier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this tends to get overlooked a lot. It's a game setting, it's intended to change with play. The conspiracies are compromised to varying degrees because it gives the players (and STs) some easy overarching goals. A single vigil can only do so much, if you can rejuvenate a conspiracy you can do so much more.<br /> <br /> The way TFV is shown kinda makes them out to be almost unrealistically nice and professional. Lots of real life extra-legal paramilitaries seem to end up either using their legal exemptions to run drugs or simply embezzling their budget. TFV seem to be good hunters if only the vampires can be gotten rid of.<br /> <br /> If the Chronicle isn't about purging Valkyrie, then it doesn't matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:33:53-08:00","id":1268808,"title":"","content":"I like it, personally, but that's just me. I sometimes toy with the whole 'Vampire Abe Lincoln' theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T06:22:06-08:00","id":1268827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268775#post1268775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters being manipulated, controlled and compromised by monsters is inevitable. But do it too much and the whole point of the gameline is lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is basically my issue, if it was just Valkyrie then okay, but Cheiron is apparently run by aliens and Malleus by a ghoul.<br /> <br /> Its a pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","name":"Apex Predator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T06:52:23-08:00","id":1268836,"title":"","content":"ghouls are still fundamentally human by a large amount. that Baudolino is also literally only guilty of hypocrisy in drinking vampire blood, blood that has kept him alive and allowing him to successfully lead the MM. <br /> <br /> it's his chosen successor who is fucking crazy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 11-19-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T07:37:02-08:00","id":1268850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268756#post1268756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a fan of that. I think part of the reason behind Hunter is to balance the &quot;Monsters Runs the Party&quot; theme in the world of darkness; to show that humans can fight back no matter the cost or consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really the theme of Chronicles of Darkness, though. Exarchs, vampires, even the God Machine, an entity so powerful and omnipresent that its only known as 'the God Machine' is not in control of things. This chaos and unpredictability is a running thread throughout the setting, even hunter.<br /> <br /> It's reflected in humanity and the Vigil by, really, the usual way.<br /> <br /> You get to choose your Vigil. A loved one was killed by vampires, you don't want that to happen anymore, so you kill vampires. Maybe you join up with a family friend or relative, find some drifter who knows about them, and you have a cell. Maybe you get into touch with a compact. They have a more focused goal, they might not be interested in killing vampires, but they can help out. But once you hit the conspiracy level, you are choosing to not go with your Vigil. You are choosing to have superiors, to have rules others made that you'll have to abide by. In exchange, you get power and influence. A member of a conspiracy calls themselves pragmatic, or a realist, while members of compacts or untouched cells might call them sellouts.<br /> <br /> And that's the human condition. Examples of it all across the board. Tier 1: You help out a homeless person, maybe help get them a job. Tier 2: You work at a food kitchen, keep people fed who can't manage it themselves, you help a larger portion of the community. Tier 3: You collect money for an international charitable organization, but only 25% of that is going to reach the people it's intended to benefit. But at Tier 3 you have a name, a brand, they have commercials, people know them, and it's easier than working Tier 1-2 stuff.<br /> <br /> It's the same in politics. It's all fine and dandy that you have strong views about how things should work, but as you move up you'll find that those strong views aren't necessarily condusive to getting what you want done. And maybe you have to kill some teenage werewolf to scratch another politicians back so he'll help you kill the covey of vampires.<br /> <br /> And religion. Most people don't join up wanting to support a child abuse coverup, but if you're the one making decisions and you want those donations maybe you can just have Father Feely discretely hidden away, and that money can go to a good cause. And it's everywhere, companies (Google removed 'Don't Be Evil' from their Code of Conduct, because there's a lot of money in being evil), law enforcement organizations, militaries, it's even exemplified in the Vice mechanic, just give in to that urge and you can get that Willpower back.<br /> <br /> Once you start going up that ladder, and let your Vigil be decided by someone else, it doesn't matter if it's vampires, mages, or some human who wants you to gank Joe the plumber because they saw something and your conspiracy can't have them talking about it.<br /> <br /> As for the specific vampires in TFV, I think a lot of the stronger complaints are a result from hearing about it secondhand rather than reading it, or people who read it focusing on one thing over another. The idea that they might be involved with vampires was there from the first book and continues throughout, only more specifically revealing that vampires steer money to it and manage to dictate some missions. They still kill vampires. They still kill other baddies. And if this plot hook is ever meant to come up, dealing with it is ideally something your players would have a decision about. Are they going to stick to their Vigil? Or are they going to go ahead and do their job like always, because without the vampires no one else is going to be throwing them money and they do a lot of 'good' with it.<br /> <br /> tl;dr it doesn't really harm any themes of Hunter, it puts a spotlight on them. And it's not some everlasting setting element, if it's something that ever comes up it's something players can deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-19-2018, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T10:30:13-08:00","id":1268900,"title":"","content":"I'ma just note that opinions don't change the fact that Conspiracies are Compromised is <i>open text</i> in Hunter the Vigil. That is the entire design point of those organizations. It can be argued that there was too much craziness going on with Monsters at the Top as the line went along for exploring that angle, but the compromised nature of Conspiracies is <i>text</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-19-2018, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T12:55:38-08:00","id":1268950,"title":"","content":"Does a Good god exist in the COFD universe?<br /> <br /> my gut tells my That\u2019s HE/SHE/IT/THEY are Imprisoned like in Gnosticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:02:40-08:00","id":1268952,"title":"","content":"There's not really evil gods. If you mean something that resembles D&amp;D's Good alignments, then you'd have the Empyrean, the opposite of the Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:24:49-08:00","id":1268957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268952#post1268952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not really evil gods. If you mean something that resembles D&amp;D's Good alignments, then you'd have the Empyrean, the opposite of the Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh ,Exarchs ,True Fae,High level Daemons.(that\u2019s what I\u2019m calling inferno Demons), Souless wolf. And several death lords","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:39:17-08:00","id":1268960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268957#post1268957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhh ,Exarchs ,True Fae,High level Daemons.(that\u2019s what I\u2019m calling inferno Demons), Souless wolf. And several death lords</div> </div> </div> </div>Exarchs are symbols, they're just the way the world is, and there's equivalent symbols for just about everything else, including goodness and charity and so forth. True Fae are alien and not really gods. Demons and angels are a thing, if you know about Inferno they're in the same book but if there's a true 'boss' among them depends on you. Soulless Wolf doesn't seem particularly godlike and was written up as more of a servant to Maeljin, who are similar to what you call Daemons. Death Lords seem to be their own thing, but they don't seem to be doing anything evil to the world.<br /> <br /> True Fae and Death Lords are both sort of powerful inhabitants of foreign worlds. They could be considered gods, I suppose, but they aren't really worshiped here, they didn't really create anything, they're patrons of their own domains and that seems to be about it.<br /> <br /> The God Machine is pretty godlike, but obviously not omnipotent. It seems to have the same problems that conspiracies have. If you go along with the theory that it wants humanity to survive (as evidenced by it focusing efforts primarily on them and keeping them from disaster) then it is split on its 'Vigil' and willing to coldly make decisions, like having John killed if it means Johns family will survive.<br /> <br /> It's the Chronicles of Darkness, though. It's not enough to just put 'Good Guy' on your character sheet. Though you can. Literally nothing in the books stops you from mowing down everyone who opposes you and just saying they were evil so they deserved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-19-2018, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:40:37-08:00","id":1268963,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Vampire billionaires! So I\u2019m keeping the backers! But we need an ancient Norse connection! And maybe the Vampires are keeping the super tech! We need that evil Vampire Luthors!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:47:25-08:00","id":1268968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268960#post1268960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exarchs are symbols, they're just the way the world is, and there's equivalent symbols for just about everything else, including goodness and charity and so forth. True Fae are alien and not really gods. Demons and angels are a thing, if you know about Inferno they're in the same book but if there's a true 'boss' among them depends on you. Soulless Wolf doesn't seem particularly godlike and was written up as more of a servant to Maeljin, who are similar to what you call Daemons. Death Lords seem to be their own thing, but they don't seem to be doing anything evil to the world.<br /> <br /> True Fae and Death Lords are both sort of powerful inhabitants of foreign worlds. They could be considered gods, I suppose, but they aren't really worshiped here, they didn't really create anything, they're patrons of their own domains and that seems to be about it.<br /> <br /> The God Machine is pretty godlike, but obviously not omnipotent. It seems to have the same problems that conspiracies have. If you go along with the theory that it wants humanity to survive (as evidenced by it focusing efforts primarily on them and keeping them from disaster) then it is split on its 'Vigil' and willing to coldly make decisions, like having John killed if it means Johns family will survive.<br /> <br /> It's the Chronicles of Darkness, though. It's not enough to just put 'Good Guy' on your character sheet. Though you can. Literally nothing in the books stops you from mowing down everyone who opposes you and just saying they were evil so they deserved it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Entities can by gods without being omniscient see The Greco-Roman pantheon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:52:05-08:00","id":1268971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268968#post1268968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entities can by gods without being omniscient see The Greco-Roman pantheon</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're just talking about powerful things, then sure there's plenty of them with Influences people would consider good. Supernal entities, spirits, goetia, guardian angels and things like that one hovering out in space that keeps us from getting hit by comets, Luna too, she's pretty nice if you're not a werewolf. There's likely even powerful ghosts trying to do nice things.<br /> <br /> A lot would probably depend on what you consider a 'good' god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:04:31-08:00","id":1269000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268963#post1268963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And maybe the Vampires are keeping the super tech!</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that not what the cut backstory was? Can anyone else remember?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:20:18-08:00","id":1269004,"title":"","content":"I'm okay with it as long as it's done with a light hand in the writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T05:43:58-08:00","id":1269192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268756#post1268756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a fan of that. I think part of the reason behind Hunter is to balance the &quot;Monsters Runs the Party&quot; theme in the world of darkness; to show that humans can fight back no matter the cost or consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but the costs and consequences of humans fighting back within/alongside an organization so powerful that it gives them anything from super-tech, to magic, to ancient artifacts is that they're going to end up getting corrupted. <br /> <br /> Large organizations get corrupted like that almost by their very nature in <i>our world</i>, and there are (ostensibly) no mind-bending/controlling/breaking supernatural powers in organized societies here. <br /> <br /> You're more than free to headcanon and homebrew your own take on Hunter, and have in run the way you want. But, like Arc said, the corruption of Conspiracies is a factual thing spelled out explicitly in Hunter books.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you really want to play Hunter, not have to change the provided fluff, but be free of being some supernatural's lackey (or whatever), just. . .don't play any of those Conspiracies. Most Compacts are free from that burden, and obviously Cells just are what they are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T06:23:17-08:00","id":1269204,"title":"","content":"Is there a reason why they can't get corrupted without a supernatural doing the corrupting?<br /> <br /> If the theme is hunters are just as bad then there's no need for a supernatural creature to be pulling strings behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","user":"Apex Predator","date":". 11-20-2018, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24492-apex-predator","name":"Apex Predator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:44:14-08:00","id":1269248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apex Predator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269204#post1269204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason why they can't get corrupted without a supernatural doing the corrupting?<br /> <br /> If the theme is hunters are just as bad then there's no need for a supernatural creature to be pulling strings behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from a design point of view, a vampire is probably easier (and probably more fun) to use as an RPG antagonist than systemic corruption. Like, if the problems with Valkyrie are just the result of it being a paramilitary death-squad operating with no legal oversight and a vast budget... What's the solution? What kind of game would that look like?<br /> <br /> If Valkyrie is an otherwise decent and upstanding organisation simply being misled by vampires, then removing the vampires is a quick and easy problem to fix.<br /> <br /> Also, the game's Hunter. The idea of the game is to hunt monsters. It makes sense then to have the problems with the conspiracy be related to those monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T08:49:05-08:00","id":1269254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Apex Predator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269204#post1269204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a reason why they can't get corrupted without a supernatural doing the corrupting?<br /> <br /> If the theme is hunters are just as bad then there's no need for a supernatural creature to be pulling strings behind the scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, VASCU, the Ascending Ones, and the Merrick Institute explicitly don't have monsters at the top, and AKD is a bit of &quot;Oh really?&quot; sort of read(vaguely surprised no one called me out on it yet).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also worth noting the relationships of power here make it more mitigated than a lot of people make it out to be. For example, Valkyrie is <b><i>funded</i></b> by Vampires, not directed by them, which means that it's still the American Government directing super-soldiers against monsters with just a few cases of &quot;Oh by the way, we also have this odd job&quot;. The Feast of Shulpae, while probably the result of Shuankhsen efforts, also realistically can't be led by them for the same reason the cannibal cult is a danger to the Arisen**. Les Mysteres gives the main credence of voice to the spirits but nothing stops individual cults in the confederacy from treating it more like an equal partnership. Whatever the power source for Malleus, it seems benign enough to just be there, and while Baudolino is definitely a monster running the show, he's also...human-enough, perhaps more so than Gallagher.<br /> <br /> Point is that there's a spectrum to these things, and there's a lot more nuance in the portrayal than just &quot;Conspiracies are monster-led organizations hunting monsters with humanity as pawns.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the theme is not that hunters are just as bad*(or good!), but that power has it's costs, change is impossible without power, and desperation opens up doors reason leaves closed. Conspiracies are just the logical conclusion.<br /> <br /> *That said, Hunters are one of the only two monsters that make a choice of being what they are, and the acceptance of one's self that most Beast's reach in their actualization definitely isn't as shady as the pscyhological steeling that comes with the decision that something has to be done about these not-human strangers-that-look-like-me.<br /> <br /> **Yes, it's been clarified that the Feast of Shulpae can't actually do their thing against the Deathless and Lifeless, making a point here, moving on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-20-2018, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T09:16:48-08:00","id":1269260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269248#post1269248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, from a design point of view, a vampire is probably easier (and probably more fun) to use as an RPG antagonist than systemic corruption. Like, if the problems with Valkyrie are just the result of it being a paramilitary death-squad operating with no legal oversight and a vast budget... What's the solution? What kind of game would that look like?<br /> <br /> If Valkyrie is an otherwise decent and upstanding organisation simply being misled by vampires, then removing the vampires is a quick and easy problem to fix.<br /> <br /> Also, the game's Hunter. The idea of the game is to hunt monsters. It makes sense then to have the problems with the conspiracy be related to those monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Valk's case more so than many of the other Monster-led Conspiracies (but not absent from them, mind), it also challenges the premise of the game in a meaningful way, setting up the very fraught and hard-to-achieve possibility (but a possibility) that a greater harmony and co-existence with the shadows that benefits everyone (<i>everyone</i>) could be made.<br /> <br /> All you have to do is drop the Vigil. It has to stop being about getting at the monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:58:21-08:00","id":1269320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269254#post1269254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">**Yes, it's been clarified that the Feast of Shulpae can't actually do their thing against the Deathless and Lifeless, making a point here, moving on.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually definitive? I always thought the Faithful's &quot;getting magic from eating monsters&quot; ritual just bypassed the &quot;Can't hold down Mummy-meat-stuff&quot;? Like, normally you can't eat Arisen, but when employing magic <i>anyways</i>...?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-20-2018, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:07:24-08:00","id":1269325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269320#post1269320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually definitive? I always thought the Faithful's &quot;getting magic from eating monsters&quot; ritual just bypassed the &quot;Can't hold down Mummy-meat-stuff&quot;? Like, normally you can eat Arisen, but when employing magic <i>anyways</i>...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's not actually written text in direct refutation, but the strict reading Mummy material still leads to that, and more importantly enough people bring it up that I just decided to cover that base despite not liking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T21:52:39-08:00","id":1269440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269320#post1269320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's actually definitive? I always thought the Faithful's &quot;getting magic from eating monsters&quot; ritual just bypassed the &quot;Can't hold down Mummy-meat-stuff&quot;? Like, normally you can't eat Arisen, but when employing magic <i>anyways</i>...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have this vague memory of CAS making some comment to that effect when the Faithful were released. Practically speaking though, you'll always ignore that particular quirk if using the Faithful in order to ensure that they are remotely compelling adversaries to Arisen (and vice versa).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T12:33:50-08:00","id":1269643,"title":"","content":"TFV's setup is one of the lighter &quot;monsters totally run this&quot; groups, its like it is halfway between a story hook and backstory. If you don't like it you can remove it pretty easy, even without making major changes to the in-universe story. &quot;Yeah, turns out we used to be basically run by vampires. We put the kibosh to that and seized all their assets. If you run into anyone who looks rich and vamiprish, tell the boss. Always could use more funding.&quot;, kinda like Mal Mal and their ghoul guy.<br /> <br /> It is basically the end result of Conspiracies having endowments. To get magical powers while remaining human/near human, humans either have to 1. Steal them from monsters or 2. Work with/for monsters who can grant them these powers. TFV is in a unique spot since their endowments are technically scientific in nature, and they don't actually need supernatural support to get ahold of them. &quot;Its super expensive&quot; explains why not everyone has their technology, and the vampire thing fits with the above prestablished theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T14:20:30-08:00","id":1269660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269440#post1269440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this vague memory of CAS making some comment to that effect when the Faithful were released. Practically speaking though, you'll always ignore that particular quirk if using the Faithful in order to ensure that they are remotely compelling adversaries to Arisen (and vice versa).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth to mention that while it was the initial response, Sothis Ascends seems to heavily hint a connection between the practices of king Unas and what would eventually become the Faithful, so it seems that the concept of mummy-eating mortals kind of grew on Mummy's writers with time (I think I even remember that the writer of that part actually said in the forums that the &quot;Unas-Faithful&quot; connection was their intention, but I may be mistaken, as it was so long time ago)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T14:49:21-08:00","id":1269671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269660#post1269660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is worth to mention that while it was the initial response, Sothis Ascends seems to heavily hint a connection between the practices of king Unas and what would eventually become the Faithful, so it seems that the concept of mummy-eating mortals kind of grew on Mummy's writers with time (I think I even remember that the writer of that part actually said in the forums that the &quot;Unas-Faithful&quot; connection was their intention, but I may be mistaken, as it was so long time ago)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the original reaction seemed to be informed by some out-of-game considerations. I know there was speculation at the time that CAS hadn't been consulted with the Faithful, so the initial &quot;Well Arisen flesh can't be eaten anyway&quot; response may have been informed by that as much as anything.<br /> <br /> It is ridiculous though. Arisen already have enemies that eat them. The Faithful were written as Mummy-eating Hunters. Any game featuring them both will almost certainly have Faithful eating Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T14:54:16-08:00","id":1269672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269671#post1269671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the original reaction seemed to be informed by some out-of-game considerations. I know there was speculation at the time that CAS hadn't been consulted with the Faithful, so the initial &quot;Well Arisen flesh can't be eaten anyway&quot; response may have been informed by that as much as anything.<br /> <br /> It is ridiculous though. Arisen already have enemies that eat them. The Faithful were written as Mummy-eating Hunters. Any game featuring them both will almost certainly have Faithful eating Arisen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in as much as anything can be about the original lines-it's also been made clear that the Knights of Saint George are designed to hunt Hunter Witches, not the Awakened, for example.(Really, the same can be said about Hunter's stuff on the whole, which is it's own whole bag of consternation and confusion)<br /> <br /> THe conflict actually <i>does</i> stem from text in Mummy the Curse as regards the nature of the Sekhem bodies of the Arisen and how it affects those who try to eat it who aren't Shuankhsen, with CAS's statements and others reinforcements of the point tying into that, but it's definitely weird and emblematic of the odd relationship Hunter has with the rest of the Chronicles world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T21:27:40-08:00","id":1269744,"title":"","content":"this is precisely why I hope 2nd edition deals with the awakened hunting situation and supplement hunter groups","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T21:37:11-08:00","id":1269747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269744#post1269744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is precisely why I hope 2nd edition deals with the awakened hunting situation and supplement hunter groups</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's no easy way of reconciling the Awakened problem without compromising on themes of one game or the other. The answers we got are actually a decent compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T06:19:54-08:00","id":1269798,"title":"","content":"The way to deal with Awakened Mages versus hunters is &quot;don't&quot;. Just use human magicians and willworkers who may or may not resemble the mages from Awakening but are approachable by hunters. Mummies might be in a similar boat but I don't really know much about it.<br /> <br /> Hunter has always been in an awkward spot as a game that invites crossover while the rest of the nWoD/CofD has progressively focused on their own themes at the expense of crossover. Mage, Mummy and Demon are probably the most extreme examples but either way we just have to roll with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 11-22-2018, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T08:34:39-08:00","id":1269838,"title":"","content":"mortal remains did a good job with how a mummy and demon antagonist would work (mummies you gotta deal with the cult, while demons are the tricksters).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> true. the hedge witches (I'm sure that's what the devs call them) have similar things like mysteries anyway, which i think you could say is like a partial awakening in some games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T09:24:49-08:00","id":1269846,"title":"","content":"My own idea is to not have vampires in control of VALKYRIE, but the internal big-secret is that just as the US props up certain dictators in the name of stability, VALKYRIE leadership makes compromises that the agents on the ground don\u2019t know about and their orders avoid conflict with certain powerful supernatural factions that uphold the Masquerade/Veil/whatever, and help take out enemies of those factions,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T09:56:46-08:00","id":1269853,"title":"","content":"my take is that the vampires funding it aren't as willing to take away their support as much as they act like they do.<br /> <br /> sure, they will take money from a cell, yet they end up giving it back once the lesson is learned. To me, the truth is VALKERIE is very effective at what they do, not only do they get rid of threats like rivals (TWILIGHT) and more esoteric threats (FORT) but also help cover the masquerade (ADMANSKI) It would be interesting see just how much they are willing to actually pull the plug before giving in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T10:48:15-08:00","id":1269865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269846#post1269846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own idea is to not have vampires in control of VALKYRIE, but the internal big-secret is that just as the US props up certain dictators in the name of stability, VALKYRIE leadership makes compromises that the agents on the ground don\u2019t know about and their orders avoid conflict with certain powerful supernatural factions that uphold the Masquerade/Veil/whatever, and help take out enemies of those factions,</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly like that more than vampires controlling them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T18:54:51-08:00","id":1269956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269798#post1269798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way to deal with Awakened Mages versus hunters is &quot;don't&quot;. Just use human magicians and willworkers who may or may not resemble the mages from Awakening but are approachable by hunters. Mummies might be in a similar boat but I don't really know much about it.<br /> <br /> Hunter has always been in an awkward spot as a game that invites crossover while the rest of the nWoD/CofD has progressively focused on their own themes at the expense of crossover. Mage, Mummy and Demon are probably the most extreme examples but either way we just have to roll with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be compromise I discussed.<br /> <br /> Back on Valk Vamps for me, as mentioned I have my own take and spiral on it. In my take on it, Valkyrie <i>is</i> co-lead by <i>a</i> vampire modernly on top of being funded by them...that vampire being Abraham Lincoln, who works to balance the interests of the vampires who fund the task force with the interests of the American government and their allies, handling the give and take of interests. This often means directing Valkyrie's manipulations of the authorities over American interest to ends he sees fit as well, while also directing the &quot;frontline&quot; efforts and resource allotment against both the worldwide Masquerade and those who threaten the integrity of the nation. Needless to say, part of this war is not going well for him. Some have to wonder if part of this is how the Beast is influencing the Emancipator's worldview.<br /> <br /> The other major leader is Shears, a Royal Avatar for Loki, who handles the logistics of the Masquerade rather than the enemies of it, keeping an eye on global and cosmic affairs and making sure that the most important directives for keeping the wool down everyone's eyes are known. His interest is more on global relations than the actual importance of any piece in it, though he does still seem to play as though America is an integral key in the puzzle. He also works to ensure the internal mystery of Valkyrie, both ensuring the dedication to keeping the things in the shadows a secret while keeping the top level secrets of the organization just that to all but the worthy.* He'll never say it anyone, but if it <i>could</i> be pried out of him, his motive is the prevention of Ragnarok. To what end will <i>never </i>be known.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Roswell happened, so on top of everything else, they have a whole host of alien technology that may or may not be God-Machine shit, which in and of itself may or may not be an infiltration attempt by the said God to control Valkyrie's upper echelon eventually.<br /> <br /> So, a little different.<br /> <br /> *The betrayal of Johnathon Kender is seemingly a significant blow to him, which makes it all the odder that Kender is neither caught nor dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T19:32:43-08:00","id":1269959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269956#post1269956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be compromise I discussed.<br /> <br /> Back on Valk Vamps for me, as mentioned I have my own take and spiral on it. In my take on it, Valkyrie <i>is</i> co-lead by <i>a</i> vampire modernly on top of being funded by them...that vampire being Abraham Lincoln, who works to balance the interests of the vampires who fund the task force with the interests of the American government and their allies, handling the give and take of interests. This often means directing Valkyrie's manipulations of the authorities over American interest to ends he sees fit as well, while also directing the &quot;frontline&quot; efforts and resource allotment against both the worldwide Masquerade and those who threaten the integrity of the nation. Needless to say, part of this war is not going well for him. Some have to wonder if part of this is how the Beast is influencing the Emancipator's worldview.<br /> <br /> The other major leader is Shears, a Royal Avatar for Loki, who handles the logistics of the Masquerade rather than the enemies of it, keeping an eye on global and cosmic affairs and making sure that the most important directives for keeping the wool down everyone's eyes are known. His interest is more on global relations than the actual importance of any piece in it, though he does still seem to play as though America is an integral key in the puzzle. He also works to ensure the internal mystery of Valkyrie, both ensuring the dedication to keeping the things in the shadows a secret while keeping the top level secrets of the organization just that to all but the worthy.* He'll never say it anyone, but if it <i>could</i> be pried out of him, his motive is the prevention of Ragnarok. To what end will <i>never </i>be known.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Roswell happened, so on top of everything else, they have a whole host of alien technology that may or may not be God-Machine shit, which in and of itself may or may not be an infiltration attempt by the said God to control Valkyrie's upper echelon eventually.<br /> <br /> So, a little different.<br /> <br /> *The betrayal of Johnathon Kender is seemingly a significant blow to him, which makes it all the odder that Kender is neither caught nor dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't TVF's little backstory of being &quot;founded&quot; after Lincoln was murdered by some supernatural entity kinda contradict Lincoln being not-murdered and in charge of said organization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T19:36:15-08:00","id":1269960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269959#post1269959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't TVF's little backstory of being &quot;founded&quot; after Lincoln was murdered by some supernatural entity kinda contradict Lincoln being not-murdered and in charge of said organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone has ever accused a vampire of being <i>alive</i> before.<br /> <br /> That said, it does a little bit, but history's a blurry subject. I ran with it being a posthumous embrace of slightly unusual circumstances. By the time it all got sorted out, the damage was done.<br /> <br /> That said, yeah, it's firmly in the realm of fanon.<br /> <br /> Well. Almost all of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-22-2018, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T21:11:40-08:00","id":1269997,"title":"","content":"Very one knows that Lincoln was A vampire hunter. maybe he became one and fact his own Death . So he could hunt Blood suckers for Eternity<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s actually Historical Footage <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AIa3jQyU1tY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AIa3jQyU1tY</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T13:01:12-08:00","id":1270183,"title":"","content":"I mean, yes, that's clearly where it stemmed from. The joke took off so well back when the movie came out and seemed to satisfy most people so much more it kind of started gestating in my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T16:31:08-08:00","id":1270223,"title":"","content":"Wait that was a actually form theory that Abraham Lincoln was A secret Vampire, hunter and people thought it was stated in a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date