Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't TVF's little backstory of being &quot;founded&quot; after Lincoln was murdered by some supernatural entity kinda contradict Lincoln being not-murdered and in charge of said organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless that is the cover story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:11:58-08:00","id":1270810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkhunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1270763#post1270763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless that is the cover story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though there's a question of why a shadowy paramilitary unit would need a cover story for such a wild event which is itself a long time ago. I mean, the unit itself wasn't properly formed till 1944.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T06:33:03-08:00","id":1270814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269959#post1269959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doesn't TVF's little backstory of being &quot;founded&quot; after Lincoln was murdered by some supernatural entity kinda contradict Lincoln being not-murdered and in charge of said organization?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lincoln was taken by the Fae. Proto-VALKYRIE took out his fetch and framed Confederate sympathizers! In 1944 the real Lincoln returned across the Hedge and took control of the occult side of the US government!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T13:17:05-08:00","id":1270912,"title":"","content":"Point is, people would rather have Valkyrie run by Abe Lincoln instead of financed by vampires.<br /> <br /> Which is <i>really</i> funny.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T13:46:17-08:00","id":1270915,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, there's that Pylon from Seers of the Throne who it's suggested may well be funding the development of the Advanced Armoury (and maybe Cheiron to some degree). Though in that case, it's not meant as a direct link so much as a natural outgrowth of the military-industrial complex. In that version, TF:V has access to their technology in part because an incredibly dodgy quasi-governmental Seer-run bank keeps giving easy loans to anyone with a cool idea for some new military tech.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, it is slightly odd that a primarily US paramilitary actually needs secret external funding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T14:17:47-08:00","id":1270920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1270915#post1270915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, it is slightly odd that a primarily US paramilitary actually needs secret external funding.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't want anyone looking at their accounts and activities, it's more illegal than most stuff. Just operating in the US would get them sunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-26T18:49:34-08:00","id":1271007,"title":"","content":"Unless they convinced congress of the reality of the supernatural but that's its own set of problems...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T01:52:05-08:00","id":1271077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1270920#post1270920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They really don't want anyone looking at their accounts and activities, it's more illegal than most stuff. Just operating in the US would get them sunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but who's going to know? Just put it in the unitemised budget. I mean that's what they do already more or less. Hell, list every sub-project and piece of tech separately. It's a joint task force so put them through different departments and agencies. Bearing in mind, that there are apparently hundreds of millions of dollars unaccounted for anyway, who's going to notice? I suppose it depends how big you think TF:V's budget needs to be.<br /> <br /> My point was following on from the discussion of the Seer Pylon. Lots of the Advanced Armory comes from wacky R&amp;D that the DoD would be funding anyway, and pretty much no one is going to investigate it. TF:V might not need as much money as it seems.<br /> <br /> As for operating domestically, just lie. If operating domestically is a problem (which I'm not convinced it is) it'll be because TF:V actually does something they shouldn't and gets caught, not because someone noticed an item in a budget, bearing in mind that they're actually still on the budget, just as a comparatively cheap item.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T03:53:03-08:00","id":1271094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271077#post1271077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but who's going to know? Just put it in the unitemised budget. I mean that's what they do already more or less. Hell, list every sub-project and piece of tech separately. It's a joint task force so put them through different departments and agencies. Bearing in mind, that there are apparently hundreds of millions of dollars unaccounted for anyway, who's going to notice? I suppose it depends how big you think TF:V's budget needs to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that TFV doesn't control these various agencies and departments. If they get money from stuff like that, it's because TFV has one or a few people in that place that can slightly influence the budgeting, but not demand anything. They don't have anyone who can say &quot;this money will go to this nondescript actor and you're not allowed to ask why&quot; nor can they motion for funding by telling the truth about what the money will be used for. That means they have to craft careful lies about sums of money that are individually so small that the people who <i>will </i>look into it won't come from high enough to just circumvent all the red tape covering the tracks of TFV. So yeah, they do tap into vast resources of funding, but have absolutely no legitimate means of actually accessing any of it and any illegitimate means are carefully calculated risks.<br /> And when estimating how big of a budget TFV needs, consider their absolutely insane R&amp;D stuff that rivals heavily funded projects of the US military.<br /> <br /> Tl;dr: You don't simply embezzle enough money <i>yearly </i>to fund an organisation the size of a <i>minor agency</i> complete with an <i>extremely </i><i>advanced </i>R&amp;D department.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-27-2018, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T05:47:29-08:00","id":1271102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271094#post1271094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tl;dr: You don't simply embezzle enough money <i>yearly </i>to fund an organisation the size of a <i>minor agency</i> complete with an <i>extremely </i><i>advanced </i>R&amp;D department.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point kinda drifted there slightly. I was originally making a point about the way it's written rather than contesting anything about how it ended up in the books. Like the R&amp;D being done all in-house is itself very odd and Seers actually gave a fairly plausible sounding answer to where they could alternatively get the technology from.<br /> <br /> (I remember hearing that the original idea was that whatever vampire was behind Valkyrie had access to superscience or something like that. So that'd be why the department was closed off)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T06:00:15-08:00","id":1271103,"title":"","content":"Putting mages behind Valkyrie is even more iffy than putting vampires there. At least vampires can be hypothetically ousted, if the enough people got wise. Or resisted, at least. Engaged with in a meaningful fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T11:44:09-08:00","id":1271200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271103#post1271103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Putting mages behind Valkyrie is even more iffy than putting vampires there. At least vampires can be hypothetically ousted, if the enough people got wise. Or resisted, at least. Engaged with in a meaningful fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, it's not claimed they're behind Valkyrie in any way. They aren't even aware of it. The pylon run a military-industrial version of Freddie Mac and Fannie May. It's a shadowy quasi-governmental organisation that funnels loans into military R&amp;D. It's suggested that potentially they've been funding the research that produces the advanced technology that Valkyrie uses.<br /> <br /> Further, it's massively corrupt and if anyone actually investigated it, there's a fair chance a large part of the defence economy would implode.<br /> <br /> Them being mages is actually more or less incidental. You could replace the board with vampires and it could give a pretty neat idea of how they control Valkyrie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T13:44:26-08:00","id":1271242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271077#post1271077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but who's going to know? Just put it in the unitemised budget. I mean that's what they do already more or less. Hell, list every sub-project and piece of tech separately. It's a joint task force so put them through different departments and agencies. Bearing in mind, that there are apparently hundreds of millions of dollars unaccounted for anyway, who's going to notice? I suppose it depends how big you think TF:V's budget needs to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who's seen American soldiers operating on American soil, who then tells their local congressman or anything. They officially have a small budget, the vampire stuff is off the books. All they'd have to do is point out that they clearly don't have enough money to have black helicopters dropping squads of armed men in the middle of the US. One weather balloon and for years people across the classes and social strati believe in UFOs, one journalist exposed the Iran Contra affair, these things happen. I do wonder if the same people upset about vampires funding and overseeing TFV ops would be as upset if they were a straightforward human paramilitary group that just killed ordinary human witnesses.<br /> <br /> As for mage stuff, they don't need a US funded special forces team. They have the the General and his entire race of myrmidons. Exposing humans to the supernatural the way TFV gets exposed to it would go against the goals of the Seers (note Division Six's lies, which wouldn't hold up against the variety of threats and people involved TFV face), and too reckless for groups from the Pentacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-27-2018, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T14:55:10-08:00","id":1271267,"title":"","content":"In my opinion TFV was privatized in the Reagan Years.<br /> Because as we all know that private industry does everything Completely better that the Government silly. Neoliberalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-27T14:59:30-08:00","id":1271269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271242#post1271242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who's seen American soldiers operating on American soil, who then tells their local congressman or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who'll do what exactly? Someone saw some guys in SWAT gear, so? I'm sure members of congress get those kinds of reports all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They officially have a small budget, the vampire stuff is off the books. All they'd have to do is point out that they clearly don't have enough money to have black helicopters dropping squads of armed men in the middle of the US. </div> </div> </div>I think that's pretty weak justification. I just don't see any circumstance in which that would work. If you have enough evidence to be asking those kinds of questions, you're not going to be thrown off by that. Equally you could pull the same trick by just putting funding under items, 'Adamski', 'Fort' and 'Twilight' on the budget and no one is any the wiser.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do wonder if the same people upset about vampires funding and overseeing TFV ops would be as upset if they were a straightforward human paramilitary group that just killed ordinary human witnesses. </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for mage stuff, they don't need a US funded special forces team. They have the the General and his entire race of myrmidons. Exposing humans to the supernatural the way TFV gets exposed to it would go against the goals of the Seers (note Division Six's lies, which wouldn't hold up against the variety of threats and people involved TFV face), and too reckless for groups from the Pentacle. </div> </div> </div>Firstly, I didn't write it, the author of Seers did. Secondly, as I said, it's not claimed they're behind Valkyrie in any way. They aren't even aware of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T18:23:31-07:00","id":1310640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1269846#post1269846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My own idea is to not have vampires in control of VALKYRIE, but the internal big-secret is that just as the US props up certain dictators in the name of stability, VALKYRIE leadership makes compromises that the agents on the ground don\u2019t know about and their orders avoid conflict with certain powerful supernatural factions that uphold the Masquerade/Veil/whatever, and help take out enemies of those factions,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Contagion Chronicle opens up the possibility that said uneasy allies are The Cryptocracy as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T18:25:58-07:00","id":1310641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1271267#post1271267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion TFV was privatized in the Reagan Years.<br /> Because as we all know that private industry does everything Completely better that the Government silly. Neoliberalism</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My timeline doesn't have them being technically privatized, but the steering committee which appoints the Director from within and he has to answer to was firmly under the control of the contractors by the end of the Eisenhower years. Ike tried to warn people...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:03:09-07:00","id":1310646,"title":"","content":"I run TF:V as being a super secret subgroup of Coast Guard special forces. This gets around posse comitatus act issues as the Coast Guard is allowed to engage in law enforcement actions within the US and they operate internationally.<br /> <br /> Weapons developement comes from the usual suspects: in house R&amp;D, DARPA, Raytheon, Boeing, &amp;c.<br /> <br /> The Vampire funding is something of a misunderstanding. TF:V raided a Vampire backed criminal op and seized hundreds of millions of dollars that they used to help fund special projects, but it was done persuant to existing law and wasn't a backchannel fund.<br /> <br /> Various supernaturals work with (or even for) TF:V, but it's not been coopted by any one group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:41:42-07:00","id":1310651,"title":"","content":"Okay, serious question: Has anyone actually <i>tried</i> playing with the story hook as it's presented? Asides from me, I mean?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T19:53:58-07:00","id":1310656,"title":"","content":"Yeah it was hilarious. Their commanding officer was -clearly- a ghoul and the players never caught on, though it's not like he was trying to have them be evil vampire slaves, they were killing giant azlu and investigating some mages and changelings having a shadow war over some magic books that were tied to a changeling loyalist who maintained his power in our world by grooming changelings from a distance before they were 'right' enough to be sent over to his Keeper in his place. Almost all of the players died, the sole survivor being the scientist who wanted to create a biological weapon that would kill vampires (who was ordered to constantly work on other things). The players then made Ashwood Abbey folks and had more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-07-2019, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T12:07:36-07:00","id":1310785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1310656#post1310656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it was hilarious. Their commanding officer was -clearly- a ghoul and the players never caught on, though it's not like he was trying to have them be evil vampire slaves, they were killing giant azlu and investigating some mages and changelings having a shadow war over some magic books that were tied to a changeling loyalist who maintained his power in our world by grooming changelings from a distance before they were 'right' enough to be sent over to his Keeper in his place. Almost all of the players died, the sole survivor being the scientist who wanted to create a biological weapon that would kill vampires (who was ordered to constantly work on other things). The players then made Ashwood Abbey folks and had more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noice.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">wordsywordsing</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T20:11:05-07:00","id":1310896,"title":"","content":"The idea of using civil asset forfeiture on the entirety of the Invictus made me laugh in real life\u2014thank you for that, I'm going to consider it canon now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T10:50:00-07:00","id":1311244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1310651#post1310651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, serious question: Has anyone actually <i>tried</i> playing with the story hook as it's presented? Asides from me, I mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it used and ignored. If you've run it - how did you present initial hooks? Did you use it for an all-TFV cell or as a mystery for a separate cell? What did it look like in practice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T16:40:12-07:00","id":1311896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1268660#post1268660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Almost EVERY conspiracy is cancerous.]</div> </div> </div> </div>...Wow, somehow I never put two and two together about just how bad the problem was. And here I thought the big three were the ones whose first editions were too weighed down with oWoD baggage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T16:46:24-07:00","id":1311899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1311896#post1311896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Wow, somehow I never put two and two together about just how bad the problem was. And here I thought the big three were the ones whose first editions were too weighed down with oWoD baggage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like it's a pertinent thematic point!<br /> <br /> (I will answer how I used the Vampire Funding in my game of Hunter, I'm just hella busy these days)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T16:53:27-07:00","id":1311902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1311899#post1311899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's almost like it's a pertinent thematic point!</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, it\u2019s a very prominent oWoD thematic point that mortals are only allowed to <i>think</i> they\u2019re in charge of anything. Luckily CofD 2e has a good track record so far of dropping bad oWoD legacy code like hot potatoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T16:55:04-07:00","id":1311903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1311902#post1311902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct, it\u2019s a very prominent oWoD thematic point that mortals are only allowed to <i>think</i> they\u2019re in charge of anything. Luckily CofD 2e has a good track record so far of dropping bad oWoD legacy code like hot potatoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an incorrect reading!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T23:43:45-07:00","id":1311998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correct, it\u2019s a very prominent oWoD thematic point that mortals are only allowed to <i>think</i> they\u2019re in charge of anything. </div> </div> </div>Depends on the edition. In the later editions it's an explicit point of both Ascension and Masquerade that Humanity precisely isn't controllable, and the conspiracies don't have all that much control. I mean, WoD has the Inquisition which was far more effective than anything we see in CofD and wasn't the puppet of anyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1311902#post1311902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luckily CofD 2e has a good track record so far of dropping bad oWoD legacy code like hot potatoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would really require getting rid of the Conspiracy setup. That'd be maybe an interesting idea, but that's clearly not happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T06:43:24-07:00","id":1312075,"title":"","content":"I'm still deeply unsure as to why it's important for conspiracies to be controlled or influenced by the supernaturals. As opposed to, you know, being organizations of hunters who scrounge up power that comes with a price and have ideologies ranging from sketchy to outright dangerous and hateful. Mortals can do awful things of their own volition and without any kind of supernatural urging. Let them. Hunter's core should be mortals taking agency, for better or worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T08:45:09-07:00","id":1312102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312075#post1312075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still deeply unsure as to why it's important for conspiracies to be controlled or influenced by the supernaturals. As opposed to, you know, being organizations of hunters who scrounge up power that comes with a price and have ideologies ranging from sketchy to outright dangerous and hateful. Mortals can do awful things of their own volition and without any kind of supernatural urging. Let them. Hunter's core should be mortals taking agency, for better or worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Hunter's dialogue concerns a circling of humanity and monstrosity as concepts and has two main avenues for that discussion. Compacts explore the completely human side of the argument, where Conspiracies explore the mixed and muddy side of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T10:25:58-07:00","id":1312120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312075#post1312075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still deeply unsure as to why it's important for conspiracies to be <b>controlled or influenced by the supernaturals</b>. As opposed to, you know, being organizations of hunters who <b>scrounge up power that comes with a price</b></div> </div> </div> </div>These are the same thing, you just rephrased them. The conspiracies are playing with the idea that there's no clear dividing line. For example, is using vitae to live forever the undue influence of the supernatural? or just the price of doing business?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunter's core should be mortals taking agency, for better or worse. </div> </div> </div>This misses that Hunter was designed around escalating tiers. That's true for tier 1 and maybe 2 hunters, but Conspiracies are <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">clearly</span></span></span> designed to represent the limits of that thinking. They're the point that you cede agency to the group in return for greater effectiveness.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you don't like it, you don't like it; the thing is, there are coherent reasons for the way it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T10:54:36-07:00","id":1312125,"title":"","content":"Hunter is about mortals taking agency. It's just that a big part of that agency included involves deciding whether taking the apple from the devil is a good idea or if it's better to fight the darkness with their inherent handicap. Also in figuring out for themselves whether that apple is an apple and if that devil is a devil.<br /> <br /> Hunters aren't powerful because they're heroic. Hunters are powerful because they're <i>desperate</i>.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, being a hunter is a bad decision overall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T13:49:22-07:00","id":1312147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312125#post1312125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter is about mortals taking agency. It's just that a big part of that agency included involves deciding whether taking the apple from the devil is a good idea or if it's better to fight the darkness with their inherent handicap. Also in figuring out for themselves whether that apple is an apple and if that devil is a devil.<br /> <br /> Hunters aren't powerful because they're heroic. Hunters are powerful because they're <i>desperate</i>.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, being a hunter is a bad decision overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shooting at vampires is always a good decision!<br /> <br /> Thing is, there are several other Conspiracies that don't have supernatural influence at all. Valkyrie is in a weird position since most of its benefits are at least outwardly tech based, and it could thus theoretically exist without the need for touching supernatural stuff at all. Making your own apple instead of stealing from the devil. It would be hard to remove supernatural influence from most other things, but it is presented as something your characters could do to TFV if you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T14:00:10-07:00","id":1312149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312147#post1312147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shooting at vampires is always a good decision!<br /> <br /> Thing is, there are several other Conspiracies that don't have supernatural influence at all. Valkyrie is in a weird position since most of its benefits are at least outwardly tech based, and it could thus theoretically exist without the need for touching supernatural stuff at all. Making your own apple instead of stealing from the devil. It would be hard to remove supernatural influence from most other things, but it is presented as something your characters could do to TFV if you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Variety&quot;. This is not a simple conversation that humanity has been having for years, and where some conspiracies should be heavy-handed with the connection to monsters, some should be light. Vampires funding Valkyrie and directing some of their target choices and otherwise leaving it at that is compromising and alarming, but it's not so egregious you can't also go &quot;Hey, is this actually a problem?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sometimes the devil isn't the devil. Sometimes things are only a problem because someone wants them to be. The inclusion of vampires as financiers isn't there to be damning, it's there to make you ask questions about whether hunting the monsters is really the point or not. It brings Valkyrie in line with the questions that Hunter is asking, rather than just being America With Laser Guns.<br /> <br /> Hunter is about taking back the night, and it's also about asking what the hell that <i>means</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-14-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T14:20:11-07:00","id":1312156,"title":"","content":"Like, in relation to this, why do you think it's such a big deal that where we discernibly know about supernatural involvement, it's in a wide variety of relationships and and roles, and how the majority of the supernatural involvement actually has a wide possibility of answers that imply different natures of relationships?<br /> <br /> Welcome to the discourse of Hunter. It only seems simple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T23:00:32-07:00","id":1312244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312149#post1312149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See &quot;Variety&quot;. This is not a simple conversation that humanity has been having for years, and where some conspiracies should be heavy-handed with the connection to monsters, some should be light. Vampires funding Valkyrie and directing some of their target choices and otherwise leaving it at that is compromising and alarming, but it's not so egregious you can't also go &quot;Hey, is this actually a problem?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sometimes the devil isn't the devil. Sometimes things are only a problem because someone wants them to be. The inclusion of vampires as financiers isn't there to be damning, it's there to make you ask questions about whether hunting the monsters is really the point or not. It brings Valkyrie in line with the questions that Hunter is asking, rather than just being America With Laser Guns.<br /> <br /> Hunter is about taking back the night, and it's also about asking what the hell that <i>means</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find &quot;partially financed and directed by Vampires&quot; to be boring and nonsensical given how military appropriations work. The idea that TF:V would be languishing without official operational funding is silly.<br /> <br /> Far more interesting a question for TF:V (and one emphasized in more than a single book) is &quot;when do the monsters cross the line?&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, the ENE might be a witch capable of powerful magic... but they're a taxpaying American citizen that hasn't actually broken any laws, is it really okay to follow the Long Night or Malleus Mallificarum's lead on taking them out?<br /> <br /> The Werewolf pack may have (literally) shredded a half-dozen people to death, but investigations indicate that the deceased were trying to summon a plague spirit and the Werewolves stopped them; sounds like they're on your side.<br /> <br /> And Changelings? Changelings are the people TF:V failed to protect and still need help.<br /> <br /> All more interesting than &quot;American with laserguns&quot; and &quot;Vampires have corrupted a military organization because money issues.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T01:05:36-07:00","id":1312255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312244#post1312244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but they're a taxpaying American citizen that hasn't actually broken any laws,</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda agree with your overall point, but that doesn't strike me as any less silly. Like, to be blunt, the American security state doesn't seem to care that much about it's actual taxpaying citizens in real life. Also, those are the moral <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">dilemmas any Hunter has, those aren't unique to VALKYRIE.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> The thing is, that's a different argument. There's a difference between the vampire patrons being coherent within the themes of Hunter and them being a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T10:42:00-07:00","id":1312336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312255#post1312255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I kinda agree with your overall point, but that doesn't strike me as any less silly. Like, to be blunt, the American security state doesn't seem to care that much about it's actual taxpaying citizens in real life. Also, those are the moral <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">dilemmas any Hunter has, those aren't unique to VALKYRIE.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;American security state&quot; is hardly a monolithic entity, but that's besides the point. The blurb you quoted is meant to showcase a new TF:V member starting their journey into complex, morally ambiguous situations that compromise their Integrity (and integrity) and morals.<br /> <br /> Whereas &quot;Vampire funded and influenced&quot; just doesn't make sense from a financial or logistical standpoint, and &quot;wrapped up in Vampires&quot; is already done by the MM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T15:19:07-07:00","id":1312425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312336#post1312336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;American security state&quot; is hardly a monolithic entity, but that's besides the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's absolutely true, but there doesn't seem much evidence that there's a section that really cares about your actual taxpaying citizens. (To clarify, I'm not saying that's a peculiarity to the US, I live in Britain, and we have our <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">equivalent</span></span></span> horrible institutions.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The blurb you quoted is meant to showcase a new TF:V member starting their journey into complex, morally ambiguous situations that compromise their Integrity (and integrity) and morals. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but that doesn't make it any less silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whereas &quot;Vampire funded and influenced&quot; just doesn't make sense from a financial or logistical standpoint, and &quot;wrapped up in Vampires&quot; is already done by the MM. </div> </div> </div>You're missing the overall point there, I agree with you, but it's not what ArcaneArts is arguing (They might think that, but we can't know without them saying so). There's a difference between executing something that doesn't make sense, and executing an idea badly. I personally think VLAKYRIE is the latter. It's coherent with Vigil, it's just not very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T09:53:26-07:00","id":1312588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312425#post1312425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's absolutely true, but there doesn't seem much evidence that there's a section that really cares about your actual taxpaying citizens. (To clarify, I'm not saying that's a peculiarity to the US, I live in Britain, and we have our <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">equivalent</span></span></span> horrible institutions.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between it being a regular problem for a citizen and it being something insignificant for an individual officer/agent/etc. Everybody has to deal with corrupt officials, but that doesn't mean every official is corrupt.<br /> <br /> The arc suggested by a lot of the TFV material in C&amp;C is, in fact, about growing disillusioned with the state of your agency and what you'll do to change it. It's literalized as vampires, because this is a Hunter game, but it is very much about confronting corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T10:09:32-07:00","id":1312590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1311902#post1311902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct, it\u2019s a very prominent oWoD thematic point that mortals are only allowed to <i>think</i> they\u2019re in charge of anything. Luckily CofD 2e has a good track record so far of dropping bad oWoD legacy code like hot potatoes.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st Edition OWoD did that. Revised edition is roughly on par with CoD. Vampire anyway, Mage is a bit more conflicted when it comes to how powerful the Technocracy is (to the point that the Revised Convention books give alternate history reads depending on which in-universe histography one puts faith in).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T12:11:50-07:00","id":1312621,"title":"","content":"You all understand that what people here argue about is as important to VALKYRIE's themes and regular player experience as the Order of the Southern Temple attempts at making prometheans to assist the hunt, or Cheiron hiring monsters, right? Like, something which could be easily removed from the the setting without any consequence on your gameplay any more than other plot hook?<br /> <br /> Feel free to keep debating this, sure, but just to make sure you all know the significance of the subject, unless 2e would do some big, dramatic change about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T06:52:51-07:00","id":1312748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312588#post1312588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between it being a regular problem for a citizen and it being something insignificant for an individual officer/agent/etc. Everybody has to deal with corrupt officials, but that doesn't mean every official is corrupt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really my issue. It's the idea that someone simply being a citizen is likely to stop the secret paramilitary member caving their face in with their rifle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The arc suggested by a lot of the TFV material in C&amp;C is, in fact, about growing disillusioned with the state of your agency and what you'll do to change it. It's literalized as vampires, because this is a Hunter game, but it is very much about confronting corruption. </div> </div> </div>I agree, I said as much on page 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T08:52:26-07:00","id":1312768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312748#post1312748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really my issue. It's the idea that someone simply being a citizen is likely to stop the secret paramilitary member caving their face in with their rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm fuzzy on the logistics of &quot;carving&quot; (did you mean &quot;cave&quot;?) someone's face in with a rifle, I can tell you that who you would shoot and under what circumstances you would shoot them is a complicated subject oft discussed by members of the military.<br /> <br /> It was also part of the joke during Jay's hiring process at MIB.<br /> <br /> If you run TF:V as nothing more than a Vampiric catspaw filled with overgeared thugs, then, yeah, there probably aren't too many constraints. But if you run them as an elite secret force made up of military and police elite, then who they're fighting and <i>why</i> becomes a lot more important.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm sure some probably don't care, they're in it to kill monsters, but institutionally TF:V canonically takes an &quot;observe and document&quot; approach until specific harm is being caused.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-22T23:43:21-07:00","id":1313794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312120#post1312120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are the same thing, you just rephrased them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re absolutely not the same thing unless you think there\u2019s no way to have powers without also having monsters pulling your strings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1312621#post1312621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to keep debating this, sure, but just to make sure you all know the significance of the subject, unless 2e would do some big, dramatic change about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the majority of Conspiracies have the same plot hook that makes a statement about the game and setting as a whole, and that statement is \u201cThe monsters run the show and all your characters are patsies.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T00:34:07-07:00","id":1313803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1268456-debate-valkyries-vampiric-patrons?p=1313794#post1313794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When the majority of Conspiracies have the same plot hook that makes a statement about the game and setting as a whole, and that statement is \u201cThe monsters run the show and all your characters are patsies.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>First, you need to define &quot;monsters&quot; and &quot;running the show&quot;. The MM, for example, are run by a ghoul- but ghouls are still human, and he is free from vampire manipulation. The Lucifuge are ruled by the spawn of the devil, but everyone are monsters and that is the point of the conspiracy. No one knows who or what pulls the strings in the Cainte Heresy. The only conspiracies which are openly controlled by some supernatural influence are the KoSG, the Mysteres, KoSA, and the Lucifuge + Otodo (which, again, don't really count). Those which are controlled by an inhuman being are the MM (which, again, I wouldn't count free ghouls), Hototogisu (again, I think he is a ghoul and it doesn't really count) and Cheiron. Those which are aware of the existence of the supernatural powers (and in some cases, those are literally Power that Be, like the Faceless Angels and the God Machine) are also aware of their manipulation, and try to work with that. And then, you have Valkyrie, who are just funded by some vampires, giving them some influence on the group but are far from running it.<br /> <br /> In short, no, monsters are far from running the show for most of the conspiracies in Hunter- I would give you Cheiron, the Mysteres, the KoSG and the KoSA. That's four. The rest are just people who are doing terrible things for very, very human reasons.<br /> <br /> EDIT- on the other hand, I won't even count the KoSG. Sure, they are influenced by dark gods, but the Faceless angels aren't really aware of their existence and are, well, gods. God may only be a monster you bow to, but they are far to high to care about you. Everything the Knights are doing is because of their own mad choices and understanding of reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-23-2019, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-01T16:49:34-07:00","id":1328831,"title":"","content":"Mild necro, but I have in a game played around with the idea of TFV being funded by a secret cabal of vampire. One of the members of TFV's director board was a Kindred who represented their interests. We got far enough the reach the reveal... but then not far enough to reach the additional reveal that their vampiric backers were themselves part of a mysterious Kindred conspiracy known as <i>VII</i><br /> <br /> That's right, the TFV is secretly controlled by vampires who manipulate them to do their terrible bidding of... <i>killing all vampires!!!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}